-- (4.1) the duty. args: an order is made under (2); the answer of the list function; the justice considers the condition is not required
#ASSERT `s 515(4.1) the justice must add a condition prohibiting the accused from possessing a firearm and the other things` TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 515(4.1) the justice must add a condition prohibiting the accused from possessing a firearm and the other things` FALSE (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 515(4.1) the justice must add a condition prohibiting the accused from possessing a firearm and the other things` TRUE (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 515(4.1) the justice must add a condition prohibiting the accused from possessing a firearm and the other things` TRUE NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 515(4.1) the justice must add a condition prohibiting the accused from possessing a firearm and the other things` TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 515(4.11) the justice must specify in the order the manner and method of surrender, disposal, detention or storage` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 515(4.11) the justice must specify in the order the manner and method of surrender, disposal, detention or storage` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 515(4.12) the justice must include in the record a statement of the reasons for not adding the condition` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 515(4.12) the justice must include in the record a statement of the reasons for not adding the condition` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

