§ `Tests -- section 515(10): the grounds`
#ASSERT `s 515(10) the detention of the accused in custody can be justified on one of the three grounds` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 515(10) the detention of the accused in custody can be justified on one of the three grounds` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 515(10) the detention of the accused in custody can be justified on one of the three grounds` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 515(10) the detention of the accused in custody can be justified on one of the three grounds` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 515(10)(c) the circumstance is one the text names for the third ground` `s 515(10)(c)(i) the apparent strength of the prosecution's case` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 515(10)(c) the circumstance is one the text names for the third ground` `s 515(10)(c)(ii) the gravity of the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 515(10)(c) the circumstance is one the text names for the third ground` `s 515(10)(c)(iii) the circumstances surrounding the commission of the offence, including whether a firearm was used` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 515(10)(c) the circumstance is one the text names for the third ground` `s 515(10)(c)(iv) the fact that the accused is liable, on conviction, for a potentially lengthy term of imprisonment or, in the case of an offence that involves, or whose subject-matter is, a firearm, a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of three years or more` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 515(10)(c) the circumstance is one the text names for the third ground` `s 515(10)(c)(v) the number or gravity of any outstanding charges against the accused that arise out of separate events` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 515(10)(c) the circumstance is one the text names for the third ground` `s 515(10)(c) a circumstance the text does not name` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- the helpers of section 515(6)`
-- "any answer holds": JUST TRUE if one limb answers yes; otherwise NOTHING if one is not covered; otherwise JUST FALSE (an empty list holds no limb).
#ASSERT `s 515(6) helper: any answer holds` (LIST (JUST FALSE) , JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 515(6) helper: any answer holds` (LIST (JUST FALSE) , NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 515(6) helper: any answer holds` (LIST NOTHING , JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 515(6) helper: any answer holds` (LIST (JUST FALSE) , JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "all answers hold": JUST FALSE if one conjunct answers no; otherwise NOTHING if one is not covered; otherwise JUST TRUE.
#ASSERT `s 515(6) helper: all answers hold` (LIST JUST TRUE , JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 515(6) helper: all answers hold` (LIST NOTHING , JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 515(6) helper: all answers hold` (LIST JUST TRUE , NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 515(6) helper: all answers hold` (LIST JUST TRUE , JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
